    "summaryAr": "Coder is the leading platform for AI development infrastructure, and we’re growing fast in EMEA. We’re looking for a demand generation marketer to help us build predictable, repeatable pipeline growth in the region. You’ll own day-to-day execution of the EMEA programs that create, capture, and convert demand, across media sponsorships, paid campaigns, vendor channels, and in-region nurture. This is a hands-on role fo",
    "descriptionAr": "Coder is the leading platform for AI development infrastructure, and we’re growing fast in EMEA. We’re looking for a demand generation marketer to help us build predictable, repeatable pipeline growth in the region. You’ll own day-to-day execution of the EMEA programs that create, capture, and convert demand, across media sponsorships, paid campaigns, vendor channels, and in-region nurture. This is a hands-on role for someone who can manage multiple programs independently, keep them running on a consistent cadence, and turn performance data into clear recommendations on what to scale. You’ll work closely with our International Marketing Lead to execute our go-to-market strategy in the EMEA market, and partner with the global Demand Gen lead, Paid Media Manager, Integrated Marketing, ABM, and SDR team to ensure every program reaches the right audience and turns into meaningful business results. What you’ll do Run day-to-day execution of EMEA sponsorships, vendor programs, and paid campaigns against the regional plan. Own vendor relationships and program logistics, including timelines, deliverables, budgets, launches, and follow-up. Research and recommend new EMEA channels, sponsorships, vendors, and campaign opportunities to test. Partner with the Paid Media Manager to launch and optimize EMEA paid campaigns, from awareness through conversion and retargeting. Partner with marketing ops to execute lifecycle and always-on nurture programs that move EMEA leads from MQL to opportunity. Support ABM programs for EMEA target accounts Partner with the SDR team to build EMEA lead follow-up plays to improve conversion rates, and use their feedback to refine targeting and programs. Track program performance against pipeline goals (MQLs, meetings, sourced and influenced pipeline, cost per opportunity) and recommend where to optimize, scale, or stop. Document processes and learnings so successful programs become repeatable playbooks for the region. What we’re looking for Based in the UK. 4+ years of hands-on experience in B2B demand generation, digital marketing, paid media, or a related field. Experience marketing in EMEA markets such as the UK and Germany. Experience managing media sponsorships, paid advertising programs, or vendor-led campaigns across multiple channels, with a track record of getting more value from sponsorship budgets. The ability to independently own programs from planning through execution and reporting. Strong project management skills across multiple campaigns, deadlines, and stakeholders, and clear communication when things shift. Comfort working with data. You can pull reports from tools like HubSpot, Salesforce, or HockeyStack, assess performance, and turn the numbers into actionable recommendations. Experience partnering with sales or SDR teams to turn marketing programs into meetings and pipeline. Curiosity about using AI tools and workflows to speed up processes, analysis, and execution. Bonus tacos if you have Experience with ABM, programmatic advertising, or intent platforms such as 6Sense, LinkedIn, CommonRoom, Vector. Experience managing programs and workflows in tools such as Asana. Experience marketing to developers, platform engineers, or other technical buyers. Experience in B2C marketing or industries outside traditional B2B demand gen. We value people who bring ideas from different playbooks. About Coder Coder is the leading platform for AI development Infrastructure, enabling enterprises to securely run human and AI-driven development workflows in consistent, governed environments. Coder provides self-hosted, agent-ready workspaces that unify developer productivity and platform governance. With Coder, enterprises can confidently evolve from human-only development to AI-assisted and autonomous workflows, without sacrificing security, compliance, or performance. Learn more at coder.com . Interview process We believe that the interview process should be transparent, consistent, and enjoyable. We value your time and hope to complete the interview process in two to four weeks, if schedules allow. Through your interviews, you will meet a mix of individual contributors, managers, and senior leaders. AI use during the interview process As an AI company, Coder embraces the use of AI tools, and we want to be transparent about our expectations as you navigate our interview process. Not permitted : Using AI assistance during conversational interviews. Permitted : Using AI tooling for take-home assessments. Please flag where and to what extent it was used in your take-home. Your submission will not be penalized for using AI as long as it is done honestly. Our use of AI in hiring We use AI tools to help manage our recruitment process efficiently and fairly. Specifically: Ashby and Brainerr help us review inbound applications by surfacing candidates who best match the role requirements we've defined. This tool does not make hiring decisions; it helps our team prioritize which applications to review first. Granola takes notes during our interview calls so our team can focus on the conversation with you. All hiring decisions are made by humans. Our team reviews applications, conducts interviews, and makes final selections. AI tools assist us but never replace human judgment, and these practices are conducted in compliance with applicable data protection, AI governance, and labor laws. Your data is not used to train AI models. In accordance with New York City Local Law 144, an independent bias audit has been conducted on \"Automated Employment Decision Tools\"; results are available for Ashby . If you're applying for a role at Coder and have questions about how we use AI in our process, or if you'd like to request information about the data we collect, please contact careers@coder.com . Coder is a proud Equal Opportunity Employer We are committed to providing equal employment opportunities to qualified applicants and do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, ancestry, reli",
