    "summaryAr": "About Us At Cloudflare, we are on a mission to help build a better Internet. Today the company runs one of the world’s largest networks that powers millions of websites and other Internet properties for customers ranging from individual bloggers to SMBs to Fortune 500 companies. Cloudflare protects and accelerates any Internet application online without adding hardware, installing software, or changing a line of code",
    "descriptionAr": "About Us At Cloudflare, we are on a mission to help build a better Internet. Today the company runs one of the world’s largest networks that powers millions of websites and other Internet properties for customers ranging from individual bloggers to SMBs to Fortune 500 companies. Cloudflare protects and accelerates any Internet application online without adding hardware, installing software, or changing a line of code. Internet properties powered by Cloudflare all have web traffic routed through its intelligent global network, which gets smarter with every request. As a result, they see significant improvement in performance and a decrease in spam and other attacks. Cloudflare was named to Entrepreneur Magazine’s Top Company Cultures list and ranked among the World’s Most Innovative Companies by Fast Company. At Cloudflare, we’re not looking for people who wait for a polished roadmap; we’re looking for the builders who see the cracks in the Internet that everyone else has simply learned to live with. We value candidates who have the instinct to spot a \"normalized\" problem and the AI-native curiosity to create a solution using the latest tools. Our culture is built on iteration, leveraging AI to ship faster today to make it better tomorrow, while ensuring that every improvement, no matter how small, is shared across the team to lift everyone up. If you’re the type of person who values curiosity over bureaucracy, and that AI is a partner in solving tough problems to keep the Internet moving forward, you’ll fit right in. Available Locations: Austin, TX Work onsite in the office 5 days a week (Monday–Friday) About the Role The Places Team at Cloudflare is seeking a skilled, operationally rigorous Workplace Operations Manager to lead daily onsite workplace operations for our Austin hub. In this role, you will serve as the hands-on operational site lead and brand ambassador, driving workplace standards, executing regional directives, and delivering a consistent, high-touch employee and guest experience. Reporting directly to the Regional Workplace Operations Manager – NAMER , you will be the operational anchor on the ground, translating regional strategy into efficient site execution. You will partner with regional leadership, cross-functional partners (IT, Physical Security, People Operations, Legal, and Executive Briefing Centers), and local service partners to maintain a highly functional workplace for our distributed team. Balancing local site ownership with regional alignment, you bring practical expertise in facilities coordination, vendor oversight, and day-to-day budget tracking, combined with a hospitality mindset that reflects Cloudflare’s values and culture. Responsibilities Lead Onsite Hub Operations &amp; Space Readiness: Oversee day-to-day workplace operations across the Austin hub—directing front-of-house services, shipping and receiving, routine building maintenance, and space readiness to ensure a welcoming, functional, and organized environment. Vendor Coordination &amp; Service Quality: Oversee local vendor performance and daily service delivery across janitorial, culinary/catering, and maintenance partners. Monitor vendor compliance against regional SLAs, run local service reviews, and provide operational feedback to NAMER leadership for contract renewals and scope updates. Site Budget Tracking &amp; Expense Management: Monitor and track the local operating expense (OpEx) budget in partnership with the Regional Manager. Review and reconcile local invoices, track monthly workplace spend, forecast site needs, and flag operational cost efficiencies. Local Workplace Experience &amp; Engagement: Champion workplace culture onsite by implementing regional programs and organizing high-touch local initiatives that support hybrid collaboration, community engagement, and day-to-day employee satisfaction. Site Communications &amp; Escalation: Serve as the primary local operational contact for Austin site leadership, cross-functional teams, and employees regarding facility updates, workplace protocols, and building announcements. Escalate site-level risks or operational roadblocks to NAMER leadership in a timely manner. Workplace Metrics &amp; Space Insights: Track, analyze, and report site-level operational data—including daily occupancy, badge swipes, space utilization trends, and ticket resolution times—to inform regional space planning and workplace decisions. Amenities: Manage day-to-day workplace food and beverage operations, including lunch catering, micro-kitchen restocks, health and wellness amenities. Internal Events &amp; Onsite Logistics: Manage logistical planning and day-of execution for onsite gatherings, executive visits, team offsites, and cultural celebrations, partnering closely with the Global Events &amp; Experiences team and local organizers. Safety, Compliance &amp; Preparedness: Serve as the onsite coordinator for facility safety and compliance. In partnership with Global Physical Security and building property management, facilitate local emergency response procedures, coordinate site safety team volunteers, lead routine drills, and maintain emergency readiness. Team Leadership &amp; Site Support: Supervise, coach, and mentor local workplace operations team members and contractors. Serve as the local operational partner for regional real estate and design teams for various hub related reconfigurations, refreshes, or buildout projects. NAMER Regional Collaboration: Participate actively in regional operations syncs, sharing local operational insights, supporting peer site coverage across NAMER, and ensuring consistent policy rollouts across the region. Requirements 5–6+ years of progressive workplace or facilities operations experience , preferably within a high-growth tech company or dynamic corporate setting. 3+ years of direct people management experience , with demonstrated success in coaching, supervising, and developing onsite workplace team members. Hands-on",
