    "summaryAr": "About Us At Cloudflare, we are on a mission to help build a better Internet. Today the company runs one of the world’s largest networks that powers millions of websites and other Internet properties for customers ranging from individual bloggers to SMBs to Fortune 500 companies. Cloudflare protects and accelerates any Internet application online without adding hardware, installing software, or changing a line of code",
    "descriptionAr": "About Us At Cloudflare, we are on a mission to help build a better Internet. Today the company runs one of the world’s largest networks that powers millions of websites and other Internet properties for customers ranging from individual bloggers to SMBs to Fortune 500 companies. Cloudflare protects and accelerates any Internet application online without adding hardware, installing software, or changing a line of code. Internet properties powered by Cloudflare all have web traffic routed through its intelligent global network, which gets smarter with every request. As a result, they see significant improvement in performance and a decrease in spam and other attacks. Cloudflare was named to Entrepreneur Magazine’s Top Company Cultures list and ranked among the World’s Most Innovative Companies by Fast Company. At Cloudflare, we’re not looking for people who wait for a polished roadmap; we’re looking for the builders who see the cracks in the Internet that everyone else has simply learned to live with. We value candidates who have the instinct to spot a \"normalized\" problem and the AI-native curiosity to create a solution using the latest tools. Our culture is built on iteration, leveraging AI to ship faster today to make it better tomorrow, while ensuring that every improvement, no matter how small, is shared across the team to lift everyone up. If you’re the type of person who values curiosity over bureaucracy, and that AI is a partner in solving tough problems to keep the Internet moving forward, you’ll fit right in. About the role Cloudflare is hiring a Head of Zero Day Engineering to build and lead the team that turns newly discovered vulnerabilities into verified protection—for Cloudflare and its customers. High-priority vulnerabilities rarely fit within one team’s boundaries. A fix may require kernel expertise, changes across software dependencies and trust stores, fleet-wide deployment, customer-facing WAF protections, and investigation of prior exploitation. You will bring those efforts together, with clear ownership from initial disclosure through verified remediation. This is a hands-on engineering leadership role. You will recruit the team, establish its operating model, and build the tooling that makes response faster and more reliable. You will combine experienced human judgment with carefully evaluated AI-assisted workflows—not automate away accountability. What you’ll do Build and lead the team - Establish Zero Day Engineering’s charter, priorities, operating model, and partnerships across Cloudflare. - Recruit, develop, and lead engineers spanning vulnerability response, exposure analysis, mitigation, patching, artifact provenance, release coordination, and automation. - Build a sustainable incident-command rotation, clear escalation paths, and effective handoffs across teams and time zones. - Create a culture of technical depth, calm execution, blameless learning, and shared accountability. Own vulnerability response end to end - Establish a consistent intake and triage process for public vulnerabilities, private disclosures, and internal findings. - Ensure each significant vulnerability has a clear owner, an evidence-based exposure assessment, and a path to verified remediation. - Lead decisions about mitigation versus patching, balancing urgency, exploitability, exposure, and production risk. - Enable the team to implement fixes directly where practical and coordinate partner-owned changes through verified production deployment. - Partner with SIRT on suspected compromise, exploitation analysis, hunting, and eviction verification. Ensure blocking an exploit is not mistaken for removing an existing compromise. Engineer for speed and safety - Drive artifact and dependency provenance so responders can quickly determine what Cloudflare runs and where it is exposed. - Build repeatable capabilities for safe exploit validation, mitigation, patch qualification, and fleet-wide remediation. - Coordinate managed WAF response with SRA, Managed Rules, Firewall/ERE, and WAF engineering while preserving specialist ownership. - Maintain strong review, staged-release, health-monitoring, and rollback practices—including during urgent response. - Turn recurring response problems into durable engineering improvements rather than repeated manual coordination. ### Develop responsible AI-assisted operations - Build AI-assisted workflows for triage, research, exposure analysis, drafting, and release tracking. - Establish replay evaluations, measurable quality thresholds, access controls, and human approval gates before production use. - Keep release authority, disclosure approval, risk acceptance, and other consequential decisions with accountable people. - Measure actual operational benefit and failure rates rather than assuming productivity gains. Set direction and communicate clearly - Define and report response metrics, including time to assess exposure, mitigate, patch, and verify remediation. - Translate technical uncertainty into clear decisions, priorities, and executive updates. - Partner with Product Security, Legal, Communications, and engineering leaders on coordinated disclosure and customer communication. - Use workload and outcome data to guide staffing, investment, and capability development. What you’ll bring - Experience building and leading engineering teams responsible for security-critical systems, vulnerability response, production infrastructure, or closely related work. - A record of delivering complex technical changes across organizational boundaries, including when priorities compete and authority is distributed. - Strong technical judgment across several of the following: Linux and operating systems, vulnerability analysis, software supply chains, application security, distributed systems, fleet management, or production reliability. - Experience leading high-pressure technical response with incomplete information, making defensible decisions, and communicating what ",
