    "summaryAr": "About the Team The Agent Identity team builds the foundational identity infrastructure that enables AI agents to securely act on behalf of users and organizations. We develop the systems that allow agents to establish their identity, demonstrate whose authority they are operating under, and securely access resources across applications and environments. Our team owns agent identity and delegation, authentication and ",
    "descriptionAr": "About the Team The Agent Identity team builds the foundational identity infrastructure that enables AI agents to securely act on behalf of users and organizations. We develop the systems that allow agents to establish their identity, demonstrate whose authority they are operating under, and securely access resources across applications and environments. Our team owns agent identity and delegation, authentication and authorization, credential lifecycle management, revocation, and integrations with external platforms. We also build Sign in with ChatGPT, enabling OpenAI to serve as an identity provider across a growing ecosystem of applications. As AI agents become increasingly autonomous, our work is foundational to how users, organizations, and developers establish trust in agentic systems. About the Role We are looking for experienced software engineers to design and build the identity infrastructure powering the next generation of AI agents across OpenAI’s products, including ChatGPT and Codex. You will tackle complex, largely unsolved engineering challenges at the intersection of identity, security, distributed systems, and agent infrastructure. You’ll help define how agents authenticate across environments, how users securely delegate authority to agents, and how agents interact with external applications and services. This is an opportunity to shape foundational technical primitives at OpenAI while helping influence how the broader industry approaches identity in an increasingly agent-driven world. In this role, you will: Design and build foundational agent identity primitives, including agent authentication, delegated authorization, and credential lifecycle management. Develop secure mechanisms that enable agents to act on behalf of users and organizations across internal and external systems. Architect authentication and authorization flows for connectors, third-party applications, and cloud-based agent execution environments. Build and evolve Sign in with ChatGPT, enabling secure identity federation and interoperability across the broader application ecosystem. Design highly scalable, reliable, and secure distributed systems that support credential issuance, rotation, revocation, and access enforcement. Partner closely with engineering, product, security, and external platform teams to solve emerging identity challenges and help shape industry standards. Drive technical direction and own complex initiatives from initial architecture through production deployment. You might thrive in this role if you: Have experience designing, building, and operating large-scale distributed systems or business-critical backend infrastructure. Have deep technical experience in identity and access management, workload identity, identity providers, authentication, authorization, or credential lifecycle management. Alternatively, have experience building cloud-based AI agents, agent execution environments, browser-based automation, or connector infrastructure, with firsthand exposure to identity and authentication challenges. Have familiarity with identity and authorization protocols such as OAuth 2.0, OpenID Connect, or related emerging standards. Bring a security-first mindset and proactively consider trust boundaries, failure modes, and potential abuse when designing systems. Thrive in ambiguous problem spaces where established technical patterns may not yet exist, and enjoy defining solutions from first principles. Have a track record of driving complex technical initiatives, influencing architectural decisions, and collaborating effectively across engineering teams. Are excited about defining how identity, trust, and delegated authority will work in a world where AI agents increasingly act on our behalf. About OpenAI OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. For additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement . Background checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct, adverse and negative relationship with the following job duties, potentially resulting in the withdrawal of a conditional offer of employment: protect computer hardware entrusted to you from theft, loss or damage; return all computer hardware in your possession (including the data contained therein) upon termination of employment or end of assignment; and maintain the confidentiality of proprietary, confidential, and non-public information. In addition, job duties require access to secure and protected information technology systems and related data security obligations. To notify OpenAI that you believe this job posting is non-compliant, please submit a report through this form . No response will be provided to inquiries unrelated to job posting compliance. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with ",
