    "languages": [],
    "summaryAr": "Replit is the agentic software creation platform that enables anyone to build applications using natural language. With millions of users worldwide, Replit is democratizing software development by removing traditional barriers to application creation. About the Role Creative is how millions of people first meet Replit, from a first-time builder to a Fortune 500 buyer. Our product lets anyone turn an idea into working",
    "descriptionAr": "Replit is the agentic software creation platform that enables anyone to build applications using natural language. With millions of users worldwide, Replit is democratizing software development by removing traditional barriers to application creation. About the Role Creative is how millions of people first meet Replit, from a first-time builder to a Fortune 500 buyer. Our product lets anyone turn an idea into working software. The creative challenge is making that feel obvious, exciting and human, whether you’re talking to someone who has never written a line of code or a CIO deciding how their company will build. We believe enterprise marketing doesn’t have to look like enterprise marketing, and we’re looking for the creative leader who believes that too. As Executive Creative Director, you'll own the creative vision for everything Replit puts into the world: brand campaigns, product launches, the website, social and demand generation. You'll lead our in-house team of designers, and partner closely with product, product marketing, enterprise marketing and the executive team. You'll find the big ideas, sell them to leadership, and get them made at Replit's speed. This is the right role if you’ve led integrated work that shaped culture and moved the business, both at agencies and inside tech companies, and across consumer and B2B brands. You can write and art direct well enough to tell a good idea from a great one, and you’d rather build an in-house creative engine than manage a roster of agencies. What You'll Do Set the creative vision: Define how Replit looks, sounds and feels across every touchpoint, from major brand moments to product launches to everyday social Lead big ideas end to end: Take integrated campaigns from brief to concept to production across film, OOH, social, web, events and paid, all organized around a single idea Raise the craft bar: Push for higher production value, especially in video and motion, and know when to push for perfect and when to ship Build and lead the team: Manage and develop designers, art directors and copywriters, grow senior talent into leaders, and hire where the team has gaps Run the creative engine: Own intake, briefing and creative review so work comes in early with a clear strategy and goes out on-brand; decide what stays in-house, what goes to freelancers, and when an agency or production partner is worth it Make AI part of the craft: Build AI creative tools into how the team concepts, produces and iterates, with a clear point of view on where human taste matters most Champion the work: Present and defend creative to executives and cross-functional partners with clear strategic rationale and conviction Required Skills & Experience 12+ years of creative leadership at a top agency and/or an in-house consumer tech brand, with a portfolio of culturally relevant work that drove business results Conceptual and craft range across verbal and visual: campaign ideas, brand platforms, verbal identity and art direction Proven experience at both B2C and B2B brands and businesses, leading integrated campaigns across film, social, OOH, digital and experiential Strong video and motion instincts, including directing higher-production shoots with production partners Track record of building or scaling an in-house creative team, and recruiting, developing and retaining top talent Experience making complex or technical products simple, emotional and accessible Executive presence: you can sell a bold idea to a CEO and explain why it matters to the business Comfort in a fast, lean, ambiguous environment where you set the strategy and stay hands-on in the work Based in or able to relocate to the San Francisco Bay Area Bonus Qualifications Experience at an AI, developer-tool or product-led growth company Hands-on use of generative AI creative tools, with evidence of building them into team workflows Work recognized at Cannes, D&AD or One Show Active Replit user, you've built and shipped something with the product This is a full-time role that can be held from our Foster City, CA office. The role has an in-office requirement of Monday, Wednesday, and Friday. Full-Time Employee Benefits Include: 💰 Competitive Salary & Equity 💹 401(k) Program with a 4% match ( US Only ) ⚕️ Health, Dental, Vision and Life Insurance 🩼 Short Term and Long Term Disability 🚼 Paid Parental, Medical, Caregiver Leave 🏝 Flexible Time Off (FTO) + Holidays 🚗 Commuter Benefits ( In-Office & US Only ) 📱 Monthly Wellness Stipend 🧑‍💻 Autonomous Work Environment 🖥 In Office Set-Up Reimbursement ( In-Office Only ) 🚀 Quarterly Team Gatherings ☕ In Office Amenities ( In-Office Only ) Want to learn more about what we are up to? Self-driving Company Replit Agent at Scale AI Adoption Build Open-Source Apps Interviewing + Culture at Replit Operating Principles Reasons not to work at Replit To achieve our mission of making programming more accessible around the world, we need our team to be representative of the world. We welcome your unique perspective and experiences in shaping this product. We encourage people from all kinds of backgrounds to apply, including and especially candidates from underrepresented and non-traditional backgrounds.",
