    "descriptionAr": "About the Team Customer Education helps enterprises build an AI-enabled workforce. We help people develop the skills, confidence and judgment to use AI in their roles, build and deploy AI solutions, and lead changes in how work gets done. About the Role We’re looking for an Enterprise Education GTM Lead to own the positioning and packaging of OpenAI’s education and enablement offering for enterprise customers. You’ll make clear how our programs help organizations build an AI-enabled workforce, from employees applying AI in daily work to teams redesigning workflows and building new solutions. You’ll define how these offerings serve different roles and stages of AI maturity, making clear who our education programs are for, the outcomes they support and how customers engage. Working with Customer Education, Marketing, and customer-facing teams, you’ll shape the packages, develop messaging and launch content, and equip account teams to bring the offering into enterprise conversations. In this role, you will: Own enterprise positioning and messaging for education and enablement that help customers build an AI-enabled workforce. Package education and enablement around enterprise goals, workforce needs and stages of AI maturity. Lead launches for priority education offerings. Create pitch materials that connect our offerings to customers’ workforce and business goals. Develop customer stories that show how enterprises build AI capabilities and achieve business results. Use customer feedback and performance data to improve positioning, packaging and content. You might thrive in this role if you: Have brought education, enablement or services offerings to market for enterprise audiences. Are a strong writer and editor who makes complex ideas clear for enterprise audiences. Have led launches and written content that improved customer understanding or engagement. Have managed competing priorities and worked across teams to deliver launches and programs. Have used customer research and performance data to improve positioning and go-to-market plans. Use AI actively and are curious about how it changes work across an enterprise. Nice to have Experience with enterprise AI adoption or workforce transformation programs. Experience developing customer stories or thought leadership with enterprise customers and leaders. About OpenAI OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. For additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement . Background checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct, adverse and negative relationship with the following job duties, potentially resulting in the withdrawal of a conditional offer of employment: protect computer hardware entrusted to you from theft, loss or damage; return all computer hardware in your possession (including the data contained therein) upon termination of employment or end of assignment; and maintain the confidentiality of proprietary, confidential, and non-public information. In addition, job duties require access to secure and protected information technology systems and related data security obligations. To notify OpenAI that you believe this job posting is non-compliant, please submit a report through this form . No response will be provided to inquiries unrelated to job posting compliance. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made via this link . OpenAI Global Applicant Privacy Policy At OpenAI, we believe artificial intelligence has the potential to help people solve immense global challenges, and we want the upside of AI to be widely shared. Join us in shaping the future of technology.",
